@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About the Hobby";
}

<h1 class="mb-3">About the Hobby: Video Games</h1>

<div class="row g-4">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
        <p class="lead">
            Video games are one of the few hobbies that combine storytelling, problem solving, art, music and community in a single experience.
        </p>
        <p>
            Whether it is exploring the open world of an RPG, working through a physics puzzle, or coordinating with a team in a competitive shooter,
            every genre asks something different from the player. GameVault is my way of keeping track of the games that left the biggest impression.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Why I love it</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Stories you take part in</strong> &mdash; games let you shape the narrative instead of just watching it.</li>
            <li><strong>Craft and engineering</strong> &mdash; behind every game is software, design and a lot of clever problem solving.</li>
            <li><strong>Community</strong> &mdash; playing, discussing and modding games brings people together.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-4">How this site works</h2>
        <p>
            Every game, genre and studio on this site is stored in a SQL Server LocalDB database. Entity Framework Core migrations create the tables
            and insert the starter data, and the <a asp-controller="Games" asp-action="Index">My Games</a> page reads it back into an HTML table.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="col-lg-4">
        <div class="card gv-card">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="h5 card-title">Explore the vault</h2>
                <div class="d-grid gap-2">
                    <a asp-controller="Games" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-outline-info">My Games</a>
                    <a asp-controller="Genres" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-outline-info">Genres</a>
                    <a asp-controller="Developers" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-outline-info">Studios</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
